Created the polyglot at `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`:

```c
#if 0
"""
#endif
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int fib(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    int a = 0, b = 1, c;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        c = a + b;
        a = b;
        b = c;
    }
    return b;
}

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    if (argc < 2) return 0;
    int n = atoi(argv[1]);
    printf("%d\n", fib(n));
    return 0;
}
#if 0
"""
import sys
n = int(sys.argv[1])
a, b = 0, 1
for _ in range(n):
    a, b = b, a + b
print(a)
#endif
```

* Python sees `#if 0` as a comment, opens a `"""` string that spans the C code, then executes the Python Fibonacci after the closing `"""`.  
* C preprocessor skips the Python parts with `#if 0 … #endif`, leaving only valid C code.

Tests:
```
python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 0   → 0
python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 1   → 1
